question/math-academy-id "q-2472" :question/problem "Find the value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x)=2x$ on the interval $[1,3].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3-1}{\\int }_{1}^{3}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ({x}^{2})|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[{3}^{2}-{1}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(9-1) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =4 \\\\ 2c & =4 \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-2472/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "86221215-32a6-5c5a-bcd7-220e166bcee8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-2472"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186101298 :question/answer-fields 17592186099389] {:db/id "q-344692/field-1/ma-v1/deb27fc54cb38444a77e3f938e41f4e4384f2ec4fff92c49acd93ba5d89d41c9/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "90e1e010-6034-58c1-8d4a-fe3c6b05416a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344692/field-1/ma-v1/deb27fc54cb38444a77e3f938e41f4e4384f2ec4fff92c49acd93ba5d89d41c9/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "fec2d609-89f1-5db6-a5a4-f9f16735720c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344692/field-1/ma-v1/deb27fc54cb38444a77e3f938e41f4e4384f2ec4fff92c49acd93ba5d89d41c9" :answer-field/id #uuid "5cb2a37e-a07b-582d-a149-401211fb4920" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344692/field-1/ma-v1/deb27fc54cb38444a77e3f938e41f4e4384f2ec4fff92c49acd93ba5d89d41c9/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-344692/field-1/ma-v1/deb27fc54cb38444a77e3f938e41f4e4384f2ec4fff92c49acd93ba5d89d41c9/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-344692/field-1/ma-v1/deb27fc54cb38444a77e3f938e41f4e4384f2ec4fff92c49acd93ba5d89d41c9/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-344692"] :question/problem "Find the **exact** value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x)={x}^{3}-3x+2$ on the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(b-a)f(c) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{1-(-1)}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{3}-3x+2)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+2x)|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (1)^{4}-\\frac{3}{2}(1)^{2}+2\\cdot 1)-(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-1)^{4}-\\frac{3}{2}(-1)^{2}+2\\cdot (-1))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{3}{2}+2)-(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{3}{2}-2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{3}{4}-(-\\frac{13}{4})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =2 \\\\ {c}^{3}-3c+2 & =2 \\\\ {c}^{3}-3c & =0 \\\\ c({c}^{2}-3) & =0 \\\\ c & =0\\,\\text{or}\\,c=\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, since $c\\in [-1,1],$ we take only $c=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-344692/field-1/ma-v1/deb27fc54cb38444a77e3f938e41f4e4384f2ec4fff92c49acd93ba5d89d41c9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-344521/field-1/7346ebe1e5d722acf040262ae8e6e53d26ca80a32da08982328df7eef98b7372" :answer/id #uuid "42cf896a-ed28-59ad-996c-fdc4c59a08f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344521/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "1df61f05-3477-592f-aa29-d9dddd2776b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344521/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd9a421f-36bc-5517-8190-6238a918c86a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344521/field-1/7346ebe1e5d722acf040262ae8e6e53d26ca80a32da08982328df7eef98b7372" :answer-field/choices ["q-344521/field-1/7346ebe1e5d722acf040262ae8e6e53d26ca80a32da08982328df7eef98b7372" "q-344521/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344521" :question/id #uuid "54fddd2c-8f80-5adf-91bc-e2f8751160b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-344521" :question/problem "Find the **exact** value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+3$ on the interval $[1,4].$\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(b-a)f(c) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{4-1}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(2{x}^{2}+3)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+3x)|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {4}^{3}+3\\cdot 4)-(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {1}^{3}+3\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{164}{3}-\\frac{11}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(51) \\\\  & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =17 \\\\ 2{c}^{2}+3 & =17 \\\\ 2{c}^{2} & =14 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =7 \\\\ c & =\\pm \\sqrt{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, since $c\\in [1,4],$ we take only $c=\\sqrt{7}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-344521/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "86221215-32a6-5c5a-bcd7-220e166bcee8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-344521"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-2490/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" :answer/id #uuid "becccbb7-7a9d-5a74-a329-bf2d3fc9abec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2490/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "76bf4f59-7ce5-5812-a44e-e3974eceff31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2490/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "c63a6d83-92cf-585e-ae9c-f7594d5c52db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2490/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "1504336f-ca72-55e7-89a2-b275c283ad75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2490/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "e0135094-0c97-5cc9-a2d3-56be05a12533" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2490/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "39f35283-6a27-5d2c-bdda-40c78280b7b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-2490/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer-field/choices ["q-2490/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" "q-2490/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-2490/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-2490/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-2490/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-2490" :question/id #uuid "7b1cbce3-95c1-5237-b1ab-a61bff4e30ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-2490" :question/problem "Find the value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x)=2x$ on the interval $[-1,4].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-1)}{\\int }_{-1}^{4}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot ({x}^{2})|}_{-1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[{4}^{2}-(-1)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(16-1) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =3 \\\\ 2c & =3 \\\\ c & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-2490/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "86221215-32a6-5c5a-bcd7-220e166bcee8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-2490"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-2477/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :answer/id #uuid "93a51178-7161-52fa-84a9-17fdb2ed959b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2477/selection/ed43d5224151224cedff9572a0bc31a320bd7a8ebd2aa526ca5884904c9d6cb4" :answer/id #uuid "0f666665-750c-5c5b-9784-8b04e6b9ec52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2477/selection/d70de39ed0e663032700fc1a4a360e6c66008c4b3951dbd32c2ad1e395b78aa7" :answer/id #uuid "8e4af557-9916-5223-83b5-ce51677c6bd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2477/selection/3bca3b7c4e38750003df6823f8a15fd4806ae33c173638520b3c8ee8cdb97636" :answer/id #uuid "608dc3e1-67e6-5c92-b661-b5c68d8d52a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2477/selection/7336f16cf9437bd809ce5e09d7dc666eb175d0cf5c31ff077c77f0542ed57f13" :answer/id #uuid "7add7088-8d49-571e-8194-c00c4decc128" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2477/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3b334d8-e5d7-5e9f-9b88-30720428ea53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-2477/selection/3bca3b7c4e38750003df6823f8a15fd4806ae33c173638520b3c8ee8cdb97636" :answer-field/choices ["q-2477/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" "q-2477/selection/ed43d5224151224cedff9572a0bc31a320bd7a8ebd2aa526ca5884904c9d6cb4" "q-2477/selection/d70de39ed0e663032700fc1a4a360e6c66008c4b3951dbd32c2ad1e395b78aa7" "q-2477/selection/3bca3b7c4e38750003df6823f8a15fd4806ae33c173638520b3c8ee8cdb97636" "q-2477/selection/7336f16cf9437bd809ce5e09d7dc666eb175d0cf5c31ff077c77f0542ed57f13"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-2477" :question/id #uuid "fdd6773f-f519-5a73-aeee-bebe69e14a35" :question/math-academy-id "q-2477" :question/problem "Find the value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-2$ on the interval $[1,3].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3-1}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(3{x}^{2}-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ({x}^{3}-2x)|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[({3}^{3}-2\\cdot 3)-({1}^{3}-2\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(21+1) \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =11 \\\\ 3{c}^{2}-2 & =11 \\\\ 3{c}^{2} & =13 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =\\frac{13}{3} \\\\ c & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, since $c\\in [1,3],$ we take only $c=\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-2477/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "86221215-32a6-5c5a-bcd7-220e166bcee8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-2477"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-3295/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "acebbec0-de5e-5291-9037-2440f4b2be74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3295/selection/593500a3db867a568918b2d1a5f966e5ba3cb22b6d2f65c83b20e9be1edb20e9" :answer/id #uuid "614db591-fff5-5c95-8b5b-00b5585aeb6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3295/selection/167ebf11c001034e2cbb5c82fd03c6c789b33fae94a34649b1567e72676329e0" :answer/id #uuid "501e7bb8-1edc-5bde-8048-14f0d2014626" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3295/selection/94786ff5da18eca7b34968478ef0ca21ee840249e1ca4e89186df64931ae3be0" :answer/id #uuid "a5071f80-8988-568e-bd4f-179679dad0b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3295/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "08f40b68-4037-5394-9f84-b3da7ec0c446" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3295/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "70015f4a-fb2e-51d4-9bbe-ecaecae11cfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-3295/selection/593500a3db867a568918b2d1a5f966e5ba3cb22b6d2f65c83b20e9be1edb20e9" :answer-field/choices ["q-3295/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" "q-3295/selection/593500a3db867a568918b2d1a5f966e5ba3cb22b6d2f65c83b20e9be1edb20e9" "q-3295/selection/167ebf11c001034e2cbb5c82fd03c6c789b33fae94a34649b1567e72676329e0" "q-3295/selection/94786ff5da18eca7b34968478ef0ca21ee840249e1ca4e89186df64931ae3be0" "q-3295/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-3295" :question/id #uuid "11f44eea-f784-5d48-abb5-d216acac4898" :question/math-academy-id "q-3295" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x)={cos}^{4}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ on the interval $[0,\\pi ].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{4}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate this integral using a substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{4}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{-1}{u}^{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{\\pi }(\\frac{{u}^{5}}{5})|}_{1}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5\\pi }[(-1)^{5}-{1}^{5}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5\\pi }(-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-3295/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-3295"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-344699/field-1/42aff35720b567089407a2a0cf7c70ff6334c9493e4d877ecdcdfa86adae004c" :answer/id #uuid "d34dcc96-12a5-59ad-aa71-0e852674d4a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "150" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344699/field-1/ae1ec0bcc83ac82fe7d363f2ad54fe23dc343f2913e126433b39173ac74d85e6" :answer/id #uuid "9fd8abde-cdb2-5b01-8878-ff82a8f75d7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "160" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344699/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "76b46926-458b-5be2-9489-1f12d1692d13" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344699/field-1/42aff35720b567089407a2a0cf7c70ff6334c9493e4d877ecdcdfa86adae004c" :answer-field/choices ["q-344699/field-1/42aff35720b567089407a2a0cf7c70ff6334c9493e4d877ecdcdfa86adae004c" "q-344699/field-1/ae1ec0bcc83ac82fe7d363f2ad54fe23dc343f2913e126433b39173ac74d85e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344699" :question/id #uuid "ee5b6f8d-9d14-51d5-8a0b-93a2327f9b03" :question/math-academy-id "q-344699" :question/problem "A biologist found that the population $P$ of some algae in a container can be modeled by the function $P(t)=150+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}),$ where $t$ is the number of hours after $9$ a.m. Find the average number of algae during the period from $9$ a.m. to $3$ p.m. Do not round the answer.\n\n${P}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since the function is valid starting from $9$ A.M., we can conclude our interval is $[0,6].$\n\nApplying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}P(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-0}{\\int }_{0}^{6}(150+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}))\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{6}(150t-\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\,t}{3}))|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(150\\cdot 6-\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 6}{3}))-(150\\cdot 0-\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 0}{3}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(900-\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi ))-(-\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(900-\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\cdot 1)+\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\cdot 1] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(900) \\\\  & =150.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-344699/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-344699"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-344648/field-1/f7c5a195b3968f28a2c36e292109faaf605e90588ff74e5a927e1dd93c4f9897" :answer/id #uuid "27b54b43-3c84-5656-be36-ea9c956fb491" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7\\pi}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344648/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "43776673-5b88-5afd-9826-30b5c8f2c3f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344648/field-1/f7c5a195b3968f28a2c36e292109faaf605e90588ff74e5a927e1dd93c4f9897" :answer-field/choices ["q-344648/field-1/f7c5a195b3968f28a2c36e292109faaf605e90588ff74e5a927e1dd93c4f9897"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344648" :question/id #uuid "752704cb-a8ad-55ac-ac26-51b58834ab35" :question/math-academy-id "q-344648" :question/problem "Find the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the function $f(x)={cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ on the interval $[0,\\pi ].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate this integral using a substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{-1}{u}^{6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{\\pi }(\\frac{{u}^{7}}{7})|}_{1}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7\\pi }[(-1)^{7}-{1}^{7}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7\\pi }(-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-344648/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-344648"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-30776/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "b99675fb-9a01-5b54-8ba3-4589872f6cd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-30776/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "6871dfb7-e709-540e-bc17-835ef63ad935" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-30776/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" :answer/id #uuid "672e9ba0-e2be-5a8f-a78a-6bb819f35c51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-30776/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "9695b549-f9eb-58e7-b607-8000ed32121d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-30776/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "f49fc375-5782-572e-8f2c-7a9cf21ca337" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-30776/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2ae9fb8-6a3d-58fa-892f-b68188b64c4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-30776/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-30776/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-30776/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-30776/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" "q-30776/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-30776/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-30776" :question/id #uuid "41a9e5db-75da-5502-afac-88828e98449b" :question/math-academy-id "q-30776" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $g(x)=2{x}^{3}-x-1$ on the interval $[-2,0].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{0-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(2{x}^{3}-x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(2{x}^{3}-x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-x)|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {0}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {0}^{2}-0)-(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{2}-(-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0-(8-2+2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-8) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-30776/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-30776"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-3297/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "2a7a1d50-db14-59be-bce0-39111903fe59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3297/selection/6e19974eead0c31037cccb7d9eb05399ff73cc4f9cbc11377b6a92fefa369d2e" :answer/id #uuid "771a42fe-844d-5583-aae9-809e4039fca6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3297/selection/fc4e157478869e2cc16df8ee4cd323015b95523464d3b9a082af315c2a4fb28d" :answer/id #uuid "7896ec0e-09d6-59e1-888e-42c8793b8da6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3297/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "c5548892-f012-5809-9df2-86631aca3325" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3297/selection/467da5e44128420eab32ba80aa1af4281aa30a9cf741846bf5be79c0af9bf421" :answer/id #uuid "6f13272c-a28d-5582-8f59-c64280b3538f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3297/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1edc742-80f1-586e-bb2b-99ecf431564f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-3297/selection/6e19974eead0c31037cccb7d9eb05399ff73cc4f9cbc11377b6a92fefa369d2e" :answer-field/choices ["q-3297/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" "q-3297/selection/6e19974eead0c31037cccb7d9eb05399ff73cc4f9cbc11377b6a92fefa369d2e" "q-3297/selection/fc4e157478869e2cc16df8ee4cd323015b95523464d3b9a082af315c2a4fb28d" "q-3297/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-3297/selection/467da5e44128420eab32ba80aa1af4281aa30a9cf741846bf5be79c0af9bf421"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-3297" :question/id #uuid "3f0b52a6-6395-5fd8-b582-320e2bab87d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-3297" :question/problem "Within  the interval $[0,\\pi ]$, determine the average value of $f(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{\\pi }(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\pi ))-(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(-2\\cdot (-1)+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1)-(-2\\cdot 1+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(\\frac{5}{2})-(-\\frac{3}{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-3297/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-3297"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-344596/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "9debab67-805d-5409-b59d-638c831040c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344596/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "c039ea78-e776-5206-8e89-f17e9e3aa758" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344596/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0b1da21-91a7-5b46-85c0-256a1c75b6d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344596/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-344596/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-344596/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344596" :question/id #uuid "bfc3ffe0-eb79-55a0-9876-0723bc5ad393" :question/math-academy-id "q-344596" :question/problem "The **exact** value of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=6{x}^{2}-8x-10$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-12$ is\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(6{x}^{2}-8x-10)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-10x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(2{c}^{3}-4{c}^{2}-10c)-0] \\\\ -12 & =2{c}^{2}-4c-10 \\\\ 0 & =2{c}^{2}-4c+2 \\\\ 0 & ={c}^{2}-2c+1 \\\\ 0 & =(c-1)^{2} \\\\ c & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $c$ is \n\n$$\nc=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-344596/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-344596"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316303/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "be20bddf-29ff-5395-9415-83419f73355f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316303/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "84c8846e-5c7f-57b1-83d0-204ab8f60e18" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316303/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-316303/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316303" :question/id #uuid "3205321e-1b1e-5760-bd45-12cdf38c44dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-316303" :question/problem "Find the value of $c$ such that the average value of $h(x)=10x-4$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $6.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}h(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}(10x-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{1}{c}(5{x}^{2}-4x){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(5{c}^{2}-4c)-0] \\\\ 6 & =5c-4 \\\\ 10 & =5c \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316303/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316303"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-344598/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "78547917-0767-523a-a258-e79f3981f9a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344598/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "37ee6230-84ad-54de-b402-7dd832678a23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344598/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ffc0bc94-8123-546e-8175-7938bf455d85" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344598/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer-field/choices ["q-344598/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-344598/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344598" :question/id #uuid "68a98d05-b09e-5226-82dd-37169f58ec4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-344598" :question/problem "The **exact** value of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=12{x}^{2}-24x+1$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-8$ is\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -8 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(12{x}^{2}-24x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -8 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(4{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -8 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(4{c}^{3}-12{c}^{2}+c)-0] \\\\ -8 & =4{c}^{2}-12c+1 \\\\ 0 & =4{c}^{2}-12c+9 \\\\ 0 & =(2c-3)^{2} \\\\ c & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $c$ is \n\n$$\nc=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-344598/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-344598"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-344574/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "bb682257-5174-5d80-b4de-46a119f65902" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344574/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "665f6f74-7c53-5525-b834-a4ef14924401" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344574/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-344574/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344574" :question/id #uuid "81417885-cdad-533c-9fc9-c94ac29cbb8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-344574" :question/problem "Find the value of $c$ such that the average value of $h(x)=4x-6$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}h(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}(4x-6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{1}{c}(2{x}^{2}-6x){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(2{c}^{2}-6c)-0] \\\\ 2 & =2c-6 \\\\ 8 & =2c \\\\ c & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-344574/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-344574"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-344601/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "0c04a6a2-8383-58d8-b809-c27bf88a46af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344601/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f670734c-e70c-5e50-9f50-eb41ca3c8b5f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344601/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-344601/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344601" :question/id #uuid "b6a588a9-c8e7-5455-809a-9dba63f139de" :question/math-academy-id "q-344601" :question/problem "The **exact** value of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=-15\\sqrt{x}+6$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-4$ is\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(-15\\sqrt{x}+6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -4 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(-10{x}^{3/2}+6x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(-10{c}^{3/2}+6c)-0] \\\\ -4 & =-10\\sqrt{c}+6 \\\\ -10 & =-10\\sqrt{c} \\\\ 1 & =\\sqrt{c} \\\\ c & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $c$ is \n\n$$\nc=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-344601/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-344601"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74170/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "d652d3fb-bc1a-5d1f-bd80-b700c5a4e5a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74170/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" :answer/id #uuid "731d0a97-d523-5c16-9bc9-98bc64e027ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74170/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "95a35b4a-070b-5cb7-a66c-13b19cacf7ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74170/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "a9fd3bb1-c5d7-5a9d-a1dc-5c59a6b73347" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74170/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "26c7a0a8-e38d-54f1-9d2b-884e1e87e0d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74170/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "47de7fae-9266-5b63-9aab-2c4fe52539cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74170/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-74170/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-74170/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" "q-74170/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-74170/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-74170/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74170" :question/id #uuid "efe91f2c-96fa-5327-b62b-92e827f654b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-74170" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/f5c51e465dd6c7b5f7a39dee26638d1704a34944b2c14eeaf2cbaf4b2a835ebe.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-5,7],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $13$, $56$ and $7,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-5,7].$" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-5}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-13+56-7=36.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7-(-5)}\\cdot (36) \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{12} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74170/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74170"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-344715/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "b7713f75-7c35-58f6-be4b-00d123d352a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344715/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f31cc2e1-7c27-5487-becd-f009ec461d37" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344715/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer-field/choices ["q-344715/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344715" :question/id #uuid "72c23b05-6d3a-58fc-8344-da3a5aa1bd2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-344715" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/dfa665cf99f35e5cd2edef04b3f334f0054bbce7fc9b66c519d59d30e77ba2a1.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[0,10],$ is shown above. It consists of line segments.\n\nFind the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of $f(x)$ on $[1,9].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{5}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,5].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=-4.\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [5,9].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{5}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={A}_{2}=6.\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =-4+6 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9-1}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-344715/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-344715"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-344708/field-1/201027ce31ae5993826403745ab80a8c143dba06e7566e11478734ebae942fbb" :answer/id #uuid "e77ebb1f-5d40-58ae-8c09-fe884701c235" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344708/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "fdc646b1-91c2-5b16-9a7c-6007e1565656" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344708/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b44e5e0-6646-5210-9d4b-630a44670bae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344708/field-1/201027ce31ae5993826403745ab80a8c143dba06e7566e11478734ebae942fbb" :answer-field/choices ["q-344708/field-1/201027ce31ae5993826403745ab80a8c143dba06e7566e11478734ebae942fbb" "q-344708/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344708" :question/id #uuid "61b15f80-13fd-5c4c-8961-5d56e0ad54f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-344708" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/c2e43e711a8c3973e080da7ee0e547b3fdec20ba4536ff7f79f21e8e4683c493.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-1,10],$ is shown above. It consists of three line segments and the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(7,0)$ with radius $2.$ \n\nFind the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of $f(x)$ on $[1,9].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{5}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,5].$ The corresponding region consists of two right triangles, so we find the total area by adding their areas:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [5,9].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{5}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-2\\pi .\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2} \\\\  & =6-2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9-1}\\cdot (6-2\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\frac{6-2\\pi }{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-344708/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-344708"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-344716/field-1/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" :answer/id #uuid "3e77f9ce-1dfb-584f-b130-3ecfc2db868b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344716/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "665b23b7-721f-5e5a-9f96-8b155585f7b4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344716/field-1/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" :answer-field/choices ["q-344716/field-1/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344716" :question/id #uuid "ba48c80d-2444-54cc-88a7-d142c12ecb2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-344716" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/101c319f12d73a4efaef385850b81b79402aaa5a1b900f1876837ff7045b0dd5.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-3,7],$ is shown above. It consists of line segments.\n\nFind the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of $f(x)$ on $[-2,6].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{2}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-2,2].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={A}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [2,6].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-4.\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2} \\\\  & =2-4 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-(-2)}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-344716/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-344716"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316307/field-1/3ab3a229b1d63f55f782989a5a2191572c52e15cef3ee349de23caec4ae46c9c" :answer/id #uuid "53eb00fe-4f55-552c-8c93-84099ec474f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316307/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "60610310-2ac4-5ae9-a341-f1deb1d8f329" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316307/field-1/3ab3a229b1d63f55f782989a5a2191572c52e15cef3ee349de23caec4ae46c9c" :answer-field/choices ["q-316307/field-1/3ab3a229b1d63f55f782989a5a2191572c52e15cef3ee349de23caec4ae46c9c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316307" :question/id #uuid "e56f391c-b858-5626-9202-9c04093762c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-316307" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/64682c2166e3f9fd2366f925330d04f95b54f370fd3d887d1d8aef8885ac35ec.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-8,4],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $20$, $80$ and $10,$ respectively (from left to right). \n\nFind the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-8,4].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-8}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-20+80-10=50.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-8)}\\cdot (50) \\\\  & =\\frac{50}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316307/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316307"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-547"] :question/problem "Find the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x) = x^2-2x+2$ on the interval $[0,3].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n       f(c) (b-a)  & =  \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n              f(c)    & = \\dfrac {1}{b-a} \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n    & = \\dfrac {1}{3-0} \\int_0^3  (x^2-2x+2) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n     & =  \\left . \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot  \\left[\\dfrac{x^3}{3} -x^2 +2x\\right] \\right|_0^3 \\[5pt]\n    & =   \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot \\left[ \\left(\\dfrac{3^3}{3} -3^2 +2\\cdot3\\right) -  \\left(\\dfrac{0^3}{3} -0^2 +2\\cdot0\\right)\\right] \\[5pt]\n    & =  \\dfrac {1}{3}\\cdot6 \\[5pt]\n    &  = 2.\n}\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =2 \\\\ {c}^{2}-2c+2 & =2 \\\\ c(c-2) & =0 \\\\ c & =0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-548"] :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x) = x - 2$ on the interval $[-2, 4].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}x-2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2x){|}_{-2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}-2(4))-(\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2}-2(-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(8-8)-(2+4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(0-6) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-549"] :question/problem "Find $c$ such that the average value of $g(x) = 3 x$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $3.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{c}^{2}}{2}-0) \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{3c}{2} \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-550"] :question/problem "The graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[1,6],$ is shown below. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $5$ and $2,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[1,6].$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/6433d1ca57ceb334f304e894e2655ef50d987567fbcf219314302bb381fd9a83.png)" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\nf_\\textrm{avg} = \\dfrac{1}{b-a}\\int_a^b f(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{6} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x = -5 + 2 = -3.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-1}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
